{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788273154592,"sessionID":"ses_fa29f8b64ffekf1eHikDs909KG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_90d846b40333425a86f2d626","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, unicodedata\n\ndef norm(t):\n    t = unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', t)\n    t = ''.join(c for c in t if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n    t = t.split('-')[0] if '-' in t else t\n    return t.strip().lower()\n\ndef load_br(path, hcol, acol, hg, ag, season, date):\n    rows = []\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n            rows.append((row[date][:10], norm(row[hcol]), norm(row[acol]), int(row[hg]), int(row[ag]), row[season]))\n    return rows\n\na = load_br('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv','home_team','away_team','home_goal','away_goal','season','datetime')\nb = load_br('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv','Equipe_mandante','Equipe_visitante','Gols_mandante','Gols_visitante','Ano','Data')\n\ndef standings(rows, year):\n    pts = {}\n    for (d, h, aw, hg, ag, s) in rows:\n        if s != year: continue\n        for t in (h, aw): pts.setdefault(t, [0,0,0,0,0,0])  # pts,w,d,l,gf,ga\n        if hg > ag: pts[h][0]+=3; pts[h][1]+=1; pts[aw][3]+=1\n        elif hg < ag: pts[aw][0]+=3; pts[aw][1]+=1; pts[h][3]+=1\n        else: pts[h][0]+=1; pts[aw][0]+=1; pts[h][2]+=1; pts[aw][2]+=1\n        pts[h][4]+=hg; pts[h][5]+=ag; pts[aw][4]+=ag; pts[aw][5]+=hg\n    return sorted(pts.items(), key=lambda kv: (-kv[1][0], -(kv[1][4]-kv[1][5])))\n\nprint(\"2019 standings from novo (top 4):\")\nfor t, v in standings(b, '2019')[:4]: print(\" \", t, v)\nprint(\"2019 standings from Brasileirao file (top 4):\")\nfor t, v in standings(a, '2019')[:4]: print(\" \", t, v)\nprint(\"2022 from Brasileirao file (top 3):\")\nfor t, v in standings(a, '2022')[:3]: print(\" \", t, v)\n\n# overlap check: how many 2015 matches match between files\nsa = set((d,h,aw,hg,ag) for (d,h,aw,hg,ag,s) in a if s=='2015')\nsb = set((d,h,aw,hg,ag) for (d,h,aw,hg,ag,s) in b if s=='2015')\nprint(\"2015: brfile\", len(sa), \"novo\", len(sb), \"exact overlap\", len(sa & sb))\nEOF"},"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 16, in <module>\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 13, in load_br\nValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: 'NA'\n","metadata":{"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 16, in <module>\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 13, in load_br\nValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: 'NA'\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, unicodedata\n\ndef norm(t):\n    t = unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', t)\n    t = ''.join(c for c in t if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n    t = t.split('-')[0] if '-' in t else t\n    return t.strip().lower()\n\ndef load_br(path, hcol, acol, hg, ag, season, date):\n    rows = []\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n            rows.append((row[date][:10], norm(row[hcol]), norm(row[acol]), int(row[hg]), int(row[ag]), row[season]))\n    return rows\n\na = load_br('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv','home_team','away_team','home_goal','away_goal','season','datetime')\nb = load_br('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv','Equipe_mandante','Equipe_visitante','Gols_mandante','Gols_visitante','Ano','Data')\n\ndef standings(rows, year):\n    pts = {}\n    for (d, h, aw, hg, ag, s) in rows:\n        if s != year: continue\n        for t in (h, aw): pts.setdefault(t, [0,0,0,0,0,0])  # pts,w,d,l,gf,ga\n        if hg > ag: pts[h][0]+=3; pts[h][1]+=1; pts[aw][3]+=1\n        elif hg < ag: pts[aw][0]+=3; pts[aw][1]+=1; pts[h][3]+=1\n        else: pts[h][0]+=1; pts[aw][0]+=1; pts[h][2]+=1; pts[aw][2]+=1\n        pts[h][4]+=hg; pts[h][5]+=ag; pts[aw][4]+=ag; pts[aw][5]+=hg\n    return sorted(pts.items(), key=lambda kv: (-kv[1][0], -(kv[1][4]-kv[1][5])))\n\nprint(\"2019 standings from novo (top 4):\")\nfor t, v in standings(b, '2019')[:4]: print(\" \", t, v)\nprint(\"2019 standings from Brasileirao file (top 4):\")\nfor t, v in standings(a, '2019')[:4]: print(\" \", t, v)\nprint(\"2022 from Brasileirao file (top 3):\")\nfor t, v in standings(a, '2022')[:3]: print(\" \", t, v)\n\n# overlap check: how many 2015 matches match between files\nsa = set((d,h,aw,hg,ag) for (d,h,aw,hg,ag,s) in a if s=='2015')\nsb = set((d,h,aw,hg,ag) for (d,h,aw,hg,ag,s) in b if s=='2015')\nprint(\"2015: brfile\", len(sa), \"novo\", len(sb), \"exact overlap\", len(sa & sb))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788273154589,"end":1788273154591}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting. So:\n- Brasileirao_Matches.csv: 2012-2022 (4180 = 11*380)\n- novo: 2003-2019 (6886) — overlapping with Brasileirao file for 2012-2019.\n- BR-Football-Dataset: 2014-2023 with Serie A, B, C, Copa do Brasil.\n\nSo three files have Brasileirão Serie A data with overlaps. For standings and statistics, I need to handle this carefully.\n\nDesign decision: I'll give each source file a \"source\" name, and unify into a Match model with fields: date, home, away, home_goals, away_goals, season, competition, round/stage, source, plus optional extras (corners, shots, etc.). I'll implement dedup logic: when querying across multiple sources, dedupe by (normalized home, normalized away, date, score) so double counting doesn't happen. For standings, I'll pick a canonical source per competition+season, or dedupe.\n\nActually, a cleaner approach for standings: compute from a specified competition+season where competition maps to a primary source. Let me define competitions:\n- \"Brasileirão Série A\" — canonical source: Brasileirao_Matches.csv for 2012-2022, novo for 2003-2011 (no overlap in 2003-2011). But for 2012-2019 both exist — use Brasileirao_Matches.csv as primary.\n- Hmm, but wait: are the two datasets consistent for overlapping seasons? Let me check a sample: 2019 Flamengo. Also