{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788273194126,"sessionID":"ses_fa29f8b64ffekf1eHikDs909KG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_ef86af44b7cf4730be7f6689","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, unicodedata\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef names(path, cols):\n    c = Counter()\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n            for col in cols: c[row[col]] += 1\n    return c\n\nallnames = Counter()\nallnames.update(names('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv', ['home_team','away_team']))\nallnames.update(names('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', ['home_team','away_team']))\nallnames.update(names('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', ['home_team','away_team']))\nallnames.update(names('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', ['home','away']))\nallnames.update(names('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv', ['Equipe_mandante','Equipe_visitante']))\n\ndef strip_acc(s):\n    s = unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', s)\n    return ''.join(c for c in s if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n\n# group by first token to spot collisions\nbase = {}\nfor n in allnames:\n    key = strip_acc(n).lower()\n    base.setdefault(key, 0)\nprint(\"total distinct raw names:\", len(allnames))\n# names without hyphen in match files that contain 'atletico' or 'america'\nfor n in sorted(allnames):\n    k = strip_acc(n).lower()\n    if 'atl' in k and 'athl' not in k:\n        pass\n# Show all names whose ASCII-lowered form lacks a state suffix and could be ambiguous\nambiguous = [n for n in sorted(allnames) if '-' not in n and any(w in strip_acc(n).lower() for w in ['atletico','america','sport','internacional','nacional','union','junior','palmeiras','gremio','barcelona'])]\nprint(\"potentially ambiguous:\", ambiguous[:40])\nEOF"},"output":"total distinct raw names: 725\npotentially ambiguous: ['America FC Natal', 'America MG', 'America RN', 'Americano RJ', 'América de Cali', 'Argentinos Juniors', 'Atletico Acreano', 'Atletico Alagoinhas', 'Atletico Goianiense', 'Atletico Mineiro', 'Atletico Paranaense', 'Atlético Nacional', 'Atlético Tucumán', 'Binacional', 'Boca Juniors', 'Defensor Sporting', 'EC Internacional SC', 'Esportivo Bento Goncalves', 'FC Atlético Cearense', 'Gremio', 'Gremio Anapolis', 'Gremio Novorizontino', 'Gremio RS', 'Grêmio', 'Grêmio Prudente', 'Internacional', 'Internacional RS', 'Junior de Barranquilla', 'Macae Esporte FC', 'Macae Esporte RJ', 'Nacional (PAR)', 'Nacional (URU)', 'Nacional AM', 'Palmeiras', 'Portuguesa Desportos', 'Real Atlético', 'Sport', 'Sport Boys', 'Sport Recife', 'Sporting Cristal']\n","metadata":{"output":"total distinct raw names: 725\npotentially ambiguous: ['America FC Natal', 'America MG', 'America RN', 'Americano RJ', 'América de Cali', 'Argentinos Juniors', 'Atletico Acreano', 'Atletico Alagoinhas', 'Atletico Goianiense', 'Atletico Mineiro', 'Atletico Paranaense', 'Atlético Nacional', 'Atlético Tucumán', 'Binacional', 'Boca Juniors', 'Defensor Sporting', 'EC Internacional SC', 'Esportivo Bento Goncalves', 'FC Atlético Cearense', 'Gremio', 'Gremio Anapolis', 'Gremio Novorizontino', 'Gremio RS', 'Grêmio', 'Grêmio Prudente', 'Internacional', 'Internacional RS', 'Junior de Barranquilla', 'Macae Esporte FC', 'Macae Esporte RJ', 'Nacional (PAR)', 'Nacional (URU)', 'Nacional AM', 'Palmeiras', 'Portuguesa Desportos', 'Real Atlético', 'Sport', 'Sport Boys', 'Sport Recife', 'Sporting Cristal']\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, unicodedata\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef names(path, cols):\n    c = Counter()\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n            for col in cols: c[row[col]] += 1\n    return c\n\nallnames = Counter()\nallnames.update(names('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv', ['home_team','away_team']))\nallnames.update(names('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', ['home_team','away_team']))\nallnames.update(names('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', ['home_team','away_team']))\nallnames.update(names('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', ['home','away']))\nallnames.update(names('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv', ['Equipe_mandante','Equipe_visitante']))\n\ndef strip_acc(s):\n    s = unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', s)\n    return ''.join(c for c in s if not unicodedata.combining(c))\n\n# group by first token to spot collisions\nbase = {}\nfor n in allnames:\n    key = strip_acc(n).lower()\n    base.setdefault(key, 0)\nprint(\"total distinct raw names:\", len(allnames))\n# names without hyphen in match files that contain 'atletico' or 'america'\nfor n in sorted(allnames):\n    k = strip_acc(n).lower()\n    if 'atl' in k and 'athl' not in k:\n        pass\n# Show all names whose ASCII-lowered form lacks a state suffix and could be ambiguous\nambiguous = [n for n in sorted(allnames) if '-' not in n and any(w in strip_acc(n).lower() for w in ['atletico','america','sport','internacional','nacional','union','junior','palmeiras','gremio','barcelona'])]\nprint(\"potentially ambiguous:\", ambiguous[:40])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788273194122,"end":1788273194125}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Very important finding! The naive normalization \"take everything before the hyphen\" breaks: \"Atletico-MG\" and \"Atletico-PR\" and \"Atletico-GO\" all normalize to \"atletico\". I need to strip the state suffix only when it's a valid state abbreviation, and keep the team base name distinct. Also \"Athletico-PR\" vs \"Atlético-PR\".\n\nAlso interesting: overlap between files is 0 with exact match — maybe dates differ (novo has DD/MM/YYYY vs other YYYY-MM-DD — wait, I took [:10] of both. novo Data = \"29/03/2003\" so [:10] = \"29/03/2003\" — full string anyway. Let me parse dates properly and compare. The home team names in novo don't have state suffix (\"Guarani\", \"Vasco\") while Brasileirao_Matches has \"Palmeiras-SP\". After norm they should match. Dates though: novo uses DD/MM/YYYY. My [:10] slice gives \"29/03/2003\" not ISO. So overlap=0 due to date format. Let me redo with proper date parsing.\n\nTeam name normalization design:\n- Strip a known state suffix: last token after \"-\" if it's a 2-letter UF code (SP, RJ, MG, RS, PR, SC, PE, CE, BA, GO, AL, MT, MS, PA, RN, PB, SE, PI, MA, TO, RO, AC, AM, AP, RR, DF, ES) or full known state names.\n- Normalize accents → ASCII, lowercase, remove punctuation/spaces? Keep spaces: \"sao paulo\". Remove common noise words? e.g., \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\" → base \"boavista\". Hmm, that's messy but rare. Maybe: strip content in parentheses, then strip state suffix, then remove common club words like \"sport club\", \"esporte clube\", \"club\", \"ec\", \"sc\", \"aa\"? That's risky (\"Sport\" is a team name — Sport Recife! \"Sport-PE\" → \"sport\", and if we remove the word \"sport\" we break it).\n\nSafer approach: alias table + light normalization:\n1. Lowercase, strip accents (NFKD), strip parenthetical content, trim.\n2. Split on \"-\" and if the last part is a 2-letter UF, drop it.\n3. Remove trailing/leading noise words only from a small set (\"sport club\", \"esporte clube\", \"futebol clube\", \"atletico clube\")? No — \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" → would leave \"corinthians paulista\" which won't match \"corinthians\". Hmm.\n\nBetter: build an explicit alias map for known messy names (a curated table), plus a fuzzy matcher (token overlap / difflib) as a fallback. Since this is a demo dataset with a finite set of team names, I can enumerate the distinct names per file and write an alias table programmatically verified.\n\nLet me look at all distinct team names across the match files to build this properly. Then:\n- canonical form: e.g., \"atletico-mg\", \"atletico-pr\", \"athletico-pr\" (aliases to atlético-pr? In 2019 Clube Athletico Paranaense rebranded; both refer to same club. I'll map athletico-pr → atlético-pr canonical \"Atlético-PR\" or keep display \"Athletico-PR\").\n- \"america-mg\" vs \"américa-mg\".\n- \"atletico\" alone (from BR-Football?) — need to check what \"atletico\" alone means there. In the 2022 standings computed above, \"atletico\" with 122 pts in 32 wins 26 draws 32 losses = 90 matches?! That's because both Atlético-MG and Atlético-PR got merged... wait no, that was with the buggy norm (split on '-' takes first part). So \"Atletico-MG\", \"Atletico-GO\", \"Atletico-PR\" all became \"atletico\" and their matches merged: 90 matches. Yes, buggy. Fix: only strip suffix if it's a known UF code.\n\nLet me enumerate distinct names. Also check BR-Football team names (they use \"Sao Paulo\", \"Flamengo\", maybe \"Atletico-MG\"?). Let me check how many \"atletico\" variants exist there.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d6374280015mbmPmyCd75V83","sessionID":"ses_fa29f8b64ffekf1eHikDs909KG","messageID":"msg_05d6304a3001KrW6QZFffFx0g6"}}
