, season, home_key, away_key, min(goals)...)... no. Keep (comp, season, home, away, home_goals, away_goals) — includes score so two same-venue legs with different scores stay distinct. Only exact same-score duplicates merge. League fixtures from 3 files merge into 1. \n\nHmm wait, but there's a subtle issue: if scores DISAGREE between sources for the same fixture (data error), we'd show both. Rare; acceptable for demo. But which one wins the dedup? I'll sort by source priority and keep first.\n\nFor STANDINGS, double-count is the real danger. I'll use the \"best source per season\" approach (most matches, tie→priority). This is robust regardless of date/round differences.\n\nLet me also verify rounds agreement between novo and Brasileirao for sanity (not strictly needed with this design).\n\nOne more design point: `search_matches` with `competition=None` searches all competitions. With team=None and just season → all matches that season (could be 1000+; limit default 20 + total count line \"… (N more matches in dataset)\" like the example format).\n\nNow — team \"display name\": show a nice display name in results. I'll derive display names from the most common raw variant (prefer accented version): e.g. \"Flamengo\", \"Atlético-MG\", \"São Paulo\". I'll build a display-name map: for each canonical key, pick the shortest most-frequent raw name? Simplest: maintain curated display names for common clubs and fall back to the most frequently seen raw name. E.g. key \"atletico mg\" → \"Atlético-MG\"; key \"sao paulo\" → \"São Paulo\". I'll build: display = most common raw name across match files (ties → the one with accents preferred, then shortest). Actually simplest robust: for each key, take the raw name with the highest count; if multiple, prefer the one containing accents... Hmm, in Brasileirao_Matches \"Atletico-MG\" appears most (11 seasons), while Copa file has \"Atlético - MG\". For display \"Atlético-MG\" is nicer. I'll do: candidates sorted by (has_accent, count) — prefer accented variant among top-count ones? Let me just prefer: shortest accented name with count ≥ 10% of max count, else most common. Let me implement a small heuristic and eyeball the result for the main clubs, then hard-fix stragglers with a curated override table (small, ~30 entries).\n\nOK. Derbies — pairs by canonical key:\n- (\"flamengo\",\"fluminense\"): \"Fla-Flu\"\n- (\"flamengo\",\"vasco\"): \"Clássico dos Milhões\"\n- (\"botafogo\",\"fluminense\"): \"Clássico Vovô\"\n- (\"botafogo\",\"flamengo\"): \"Clássico da Rivalidade\"\n- (\"vasco\",\"botafogo\"): \"Clássico dos Gigantes\"? — hmm I'm fairly sure Vasco×Botafogo doesn't have a super-canonical name... Actually it's sometimes \"Clássico dos Gigantes\". I'll include it.\n- (\"gremio\",\"internacional\"): \"Gre-Nal\"\n- (\"corinthians\",\"sao paulo\"): \"Clássico Majestoso\" (a.k.a. \"Majestoso\")\n- (\"sao paulo\",\"santos\"): \"Choque-Rei\"\n- (\"corinthians\",\"palmeiras\"): \"O Derby\" (Derby Paulista)\n- (\"palmeiras\",\"santos\"): \"Clássico da Saudade\"\n- (\"atletico mg\",\"cruzeiro\"): \"Clássico Mineiro\"\n- (\"atletico mg\",\"america mg\"): \"Clássico das Multidões\" — hmm, that's actually the name for Sport×Santa Cruz in Pernambuco. Atlético-MG×América-MG is \"Clássico das Multidões\"? Let me think... Clássico das Multidões = Atlético-MG vs América-MG? No... I recall Sport vs Santa Cruz = \"Clássico das Multidões\". And Atlético vs América = \"Clássico das Multidões\" also gets used in MG (\"o clássico das multidões mineiro\")... I'm not 100% sure. To be safe I'll use fewer, well-established names:\n  - (\"bahia\",\"vitoria\"): \"Ba-Vi\"\n  - (\"sport\",\"nautico\"): \"Clássico dos Clássicos\"\n  - (\"sport\",\"santa cruz\"): \"Clássico das Multidões\"\n  - (\"nautico\",\"santa cruz\"): \"Clássico dos Emoções\"\n  - (\"coritiba\",\"atletico pr\"): \"Atletiba\"\n  - (\"ceara\",\"fortaleza\"): \"Clássico-Rei\"\n  - (\"remo\",\"paysandu\"): \"Re-Pa\"\n  - (\"avai\",\"figueirense\"): \"Clássico de Florianópolis\"\n  - (\"goias\",\"vila nova\"): \"Clássico Goiano\" — hmm \"Derby do Cerrado\"? Goiás×Vila Nova is \"Clássico Goiano\" (or \"Clássico do Cerrado\" is Goiás vs... I'll use \"Clássico Goiano\").\n  - (\"atletico mg\",\"america mg\"): \"Clássico Mineiro\" is Atlético×Cruzeiro; for Atlético×América I'll skip.\n  - (\"cruzeiro\",\"america mg\")? skip.\n  - (\"vasco\",\"fluminense\"): \"Clássico dos Gigantes\"? Hmm. Fluminense×Vasco... I'm not certain. Skip to be safe. Actually — wait, I should double check \"Clássico dos Gigantes\" = Botafogo×Vasco. Yes, that one I'm confident about (it commemorates... it's a known Rio derby name). Keep.\n  - (\"coritiba\",\"parana\"): \"Coritibanão\"? skip. (\"atletico pr\",\"parana\"): \"Paratiba\" — known. Include.\n  - (\"abc\",\"america rn\")? \"Clássico de Natal\"? Not needed.\n\nGood enough — 17 derbies.\n\n\"Compare Palmeiras and Santos head-to-head\" → head_to_head tool.\n\"Compare the 2018 and 2019 seasons\" → season comparison: average_goals per season + standings top 3 + champion. I'll add a tool `season_comparison(competition, season_a, season_b)`? That's very specific. Or `average_goals` with season param covers the numbers; and standings per season. Hmm, \"At least 20 sample questions can be answered\" — I'll write a SAMPLE_QUESTIONS list in README with the 20+ questions and which tool answers each. A `season_comparison` convenience tool would make that one question one-call — I'll add it (goals avg, home win rate, top 3 teams, champion, biggest win).\n\nNow the tool for \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\": search_matches with stage=\"final\" works for Libertadores (stage col); for Copa do Brasil, \"round 8\" = final — I'll add a `stage` param that matches stage OR round; and in the Copa loader, map round 8 → stage \"final\", round 7 → \"semifinal\", round 6 → \"quarterfinal\", round 5 → \"round of 16\" — WAIT is that right? Copa do Brasil format: Round 1 (80 teams), Round 2 (40), Round 3 (20 → 10), Round of 16 (16 teams), Quarterfinals, Semifinals, Final. Hmm — rounds 1-8 in the data: after round 3 there might be a playoff... Modern format: 1st round, 2nd round, 3rd round, round of 16, QF, SF, Final = 7 rounds. This data has 8 rounds for 2012-2013? Different formats per year. I should NOT hardcode round→stage for all seasons. Instead: label rounds literally (\"Round 8\") but ALSO compute \"final = max round of season\" for champion determination. For the \"find finals\" query, I'll support stage=\"final\" meaning: Libertadores stage==\"final\"; Copa do Brasil round == max round of that season (or \"Round 8\"-ish). Hmm — tricky for multi-season queries where max round differs by season. \n\nSimpler: in the Copa loader, set stage = f\"round {n}\" but ALSO if round == 8 → \"final\" when season format has 8 rounds... Let me check by season which max rounds exist: 2012:? Let me compute quickly. If max round per season is consistently 8 (or 7), then map: last round → \"final\", second-to-last → \"semifinal\". Let me check the data.\n\nAlso Libertadores stage values: group stage, round of 16, quarterfinals, semifinals, final. Good.\n\nLet me check Copa max round per season.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d67cb6b001ArJU8LXF4S5bc1","sessionID":"ses_fa29f8b64ffekf1eHikDs909KG","messageID":"msg_05d6673d5001N6NgmahGo6eMPj"}}
