 377 + Serie B 380 + Serie C 215 + Copa 116 = 1088. Yes. My bad.\n\nAlso important: novo vs brfile common fixtures = only 30?! But both files have 380 matches for 2015 Serie A. The (season, home, away) key should match 380 fixtures... unless team keys differ! E.g., novo \"Grêmio\" → \"gremio\" vs brfile \"Grêmio\"... wait both → \"gremio\". Only 30 common?! Something's off. Let me investigate — maybe novo's home/away are swapped, or names differ substantially (\"Atletico-MG\" vs \"Atlético Mineiro\"? no...). Let me debug by listing some 2015 fixtures from each.\n\nWait — actually, could it be that ma dict keys (s,h,aw) — for novo I parse Data → brd gives ISO? \"29/03/2003\" → dd/mm/yy → \"2003-03-29\" ✓. Season from d[:4] ✓. Hmm let me debug.\n\nAlso BRFB vs brfile: 16 common, 15 agree — again low. BRFB 2015 Serie A: 378 matches, brfile 380 → should be ~378 common. Something's wrong with my key matching — e.g. BRFB \"Atletico Mineiro\" (full name!) → slug \"atletico mineiro\" — toks[-1]=\"mineiro\" not UF → key \"atletico mineiro\" ≠ \"atletico mg\". Right! BRFB uses \"Atletico Mineiro\", \"Atletico Goianiense\", \"Atletico Paranaense\", \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\", \"Sport Recife\", etc. — my alias layer wasn't applied in this probe (only BASES suffix-drop). That explains low overlap for teams like Atlético-MG. But novo uses \"Athletico-PR\"?? and brfile \"Atletico-PR\"... both → \"atletico pr\" ✓ should match...\n\nHmm wait, novo vs brfile only 30 common. Let me debug specifically: 2015 Serie A fixtures in each, compare a few team keys.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d6a3f7a001nvDVaOoWr4EquP","sessionID":"ses_fa29f8b64ffekf1eHikDs909KG","messageID":"msg_05d69f448001iuzOKSACulpiDx"}}
