{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788273988286,"sessionID":"ses_fa29f8b64ffekf1eHikDs909KG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_a50313b1864e4a809e84c48d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, unicodedata, re\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nUF = {'SP','RJ','MG','RS','PR','SC','PE','CE','BA','GO','AL','MT','MS','PA','RN','PB','SE','PI','MA','TO','RO','AC','AM','AP','RR','DF','ES'}\ndef slug(s):\n    s = unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', s)\n    s = ''.join(c for c in s if not unicodedata.combining(c)).lower()\n    m = re.findall(r'\\(([^)]*)\\)', s)\n    s = re.sub(r'\\([^)]*\\)', ' ', s)\n    for x in m:\n        x = x.strip()\n        if x and len(x.split()) == 1 and len(x) <= 4: s += ' ' + x\n    s = ''.join(c if c.isalnum() else ' ' for c in s)\n    return ' '.join(s.split())\n\nALIASES = {\n    'atletico mineiro': 'atletico mg', 'atletico mineiro mg': 'atletico mg', 'clube atletico mineiro': 'atletico mg',\n    'atletico goianiense': 'atletico go', 'atletico goianiense go': 'atletico go',\n    'atletico paranaense': 'atletico pr', 'atletico paranaense pr': 'atletico pr',\n    'athletico paranaense': 'atletico pr', 'athletico paranaense pr': 'atletico pr', 'athletico pr': 'atletico pr', 'athletico': 'atletico pr',\n    'sport recife': 'sport', 'sport club do recife': 'sport', 'sport recife pe': 'sport',\n    'ceara sporting club': 'ceara', 'ceara sc': 'ceara', 'clube do remo': 'remo',\n    'nautico capibaribe': 'nautico', 'nautico capibaribe pe': 'nautico',\n    'vasco da gama': 'vasco', 'vasco da gama rj': 'vasco', 'cs alagoano': 'csa', 'cs sergipe': 'sergipe',\n    'boavista sport club': 'boavista', 'boavista sport club rj': 'boavista', 'boavista sc saquarema': 'boavista',\n    'gremio rs': 'gremio', 'internacional rs': 'internacional',\n    'vitoria ec': 'vitoria ba', 'ec vitoria': 'vitoria ba', 'vitoria': 'vitoria ba', 'ec bahia': 'bahia',\n    'red bull bragantino': 'bragantino', 'rb bragantino': 'bragantino', 'red bull bragantino sp': 'bragantino',\n    'botafogo': 'botafogo rj', 'sport club corinthians paulista': 'corinthians', 'spfc': 'sao paulo',\n    'parana clube': 'parana', 'santa cruz fc': 'santa cruz', 'aa ponte preta': 'ponte preta',\n    'america fc natal': 'america rn', 'novorizontino': 'novorizontino', 'gremio novorizontino': 'novorizontino',\n    'athletic club': 'athletic mg', 'fortaleza ec': 'fortaleza', 'fortaleza fc': 'fortaleza',\n    'sao jose poa': 'sao jose rs', 'operario fc ms': 'operario ms', 'ad confianca': 'confianca',\n    'vila nova fc': 'vila nova', 'sampaio correa ma': 'sampaio correa',\n}\nBASES = {'palmeiras','flamengo','corinthians','santos','sao paulo','sport','bahia','ceara','fortaleza','cruzeiro','coritiba','parana','chapecoense','avai','figueirense','criciuma','goias','gremio','internacional','fluminense','guarani','portuguesa','juventude','caxias','nautico','remo','paysandu','sampaio correa','csa','crb','abc','vasco','vila nova','ponte preta','santa cruz','joinville','bragantino','america rn','confianca','operario ms'}\ndef key(t):\n    s = slug(t)\n    if s in ALIASES: return ALIASES[s]\n    toks = s.split()\n    if toks and toks[-1].upper() in UF:\n        base = ' '.join(toks[:-1])\n        if base in BASES: return base\n    return s\n\ndef load(path, hcol, acol, hg, ag, dcol, dparse, scol=None, tcol=None, tval=None, comp=None):\n    rows = []\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n            if tcol and row[tcol] != tval: continue\n            try:\n                hgi, agi = int(float(row[hg])), int(float(row[ag]))\n            except (ValueError, TypeError):\n                hgi = agi = None\n            d = dparse(row[dcol]) if row[dcol] else None\n            s = int(row[scol]) if scol and row[scol] not in ('','NA') else (int(d[:4]) if d else None)\n            if s is None: continue\n            rows.append((d, key(row[hcol]), key(row[acol]), hgi, agi, s, comp))\n    return rows\n\ndef iso(d): return d[:10]\ndef brd(d):\n    dd, mm, yy = d.split('/'); return f\"{yy}-{mm}-{dd}\"\n\nmatches = []\nmatches += load('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv','home_team','away_team','home_goal','away_goal','datetime',iso,scol='season',comp='Serie A')\nmatches += load('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv','home_team','away_team','home_goal','away_goal','datetime',iso,scol='season',comp='Copa do Brasil')\nmatches += load('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv','home_team','away_team','home_goal','away_goal','datetime',iso,scol='season',comp='Libertadores')\nmatches += load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv','home','away','home_goal','away_goal','date',iso,tcol='tournament',comp=None)  # per-tournament below\n\nwith open('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n        try:\n            hgi, agi = int(float(row['home_goal'])), int(float(row['away_goal']))\n        except (ValueError, TypeError):\n            hgi = agi = None\n        d = row['date'][:10]\n        matches.append((d, key(row['home']), key(row['away']), hgi, agi, int(d[:4]), row['tournament']))\n\nmatches += load('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv','Equipe_mandante','Equipe_visitante','Gols_mandante','Gols_visitante','Data',brd,scol='Ano',comp='Serie A')\nprint(\"total matches:\", len(matches))\n\n# biggest wins (scored, all comps)\nscored = [m for m in matches if m[3] is not None]\nbig = sorted(scored, key=lambda m: (-abs(m[3]-m[4]), -(m[3]+m[4])))[:8]\nfor b in big: print(\"BIG:\", b)\n\n# Fla-Flu h2h (all comps, dedup by season/home/away/score)\nseen = set(); h2h = []\nfor m in matches:\n    if {m[1],m[2]} == {'flamengo','fluminense'}:\n        k = (m[5], m[1], m[2], m[3], m[4], m[6])\n        if k in seen: continue\n        seen.add(k); h2h.append(m)\nfla = sum(1 for m in h2h if (m[1]=='flamengo' and m[3]>m[4]) or (m[2]=='flamengo' and m[4]>m[3]))\nflu = sum(1 for m in h2h if (m[1]=='fluminense' and m[3]>m[4]) or (m[2]=='fluminense' and m[4]>m[3]))\ndr = len(h2h) - fla - flu\nprint(f\"Fla-Flu: {len(h2h)} matches, Flamengo {fla}, Fluminense {flu}, draws {dr}\")\n\n# Corinthians home 2022 (Serie A from brfile only)\ncor = [m for m in matches if m[6]=='Serie A' and m[5]==2022 and m[1]=='corinthians' and m[3] is not None and m[0] and m[0]<'2023' and m[0]>='2022']\n# oops brfile rows only - need source tracking; skip precision, just count from brfile-style: use season col rounds... let me just count home wins for corinthians 2022 from brfile alone\nEOF"},"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 68, in <module>\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 56, in load\nValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: 'NA'\n","metadata":{"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 68, in <module>\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 56, in load\nValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: 'NA'\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, unicodedata, re\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nUF = {'SP','RJ','MG','RS','PR','SC','PE','CE','BA','GO','AL','MT','MS','PA','RN','PB','SE','PI','MA','TO','RO','AC','AM','AP','RR','DF','ES'}\ndef slug(s):\n    s = unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', s)\n    s = ''.join(c for c in s if not unicodedata.combining(c)).lower()\n    m = re.findall(r'\\(([^)]*)\\)', s)\n    s = re.sub(r'\\([^)]*\\)', ' ', s)\n    for x in m:\n        x = x.strip()\n        if x and len(x.split()) == 1 and len(x) <= 4: s += ' ' + x\n    s = ''.join(c if c.isalnum() else ' ' for c in s)\n    return ' '.join(s.split())\n\nALIASES = {\n    'atletico mineiro': 'atletico mg', 'atletico mineiro mg': 'atletico mg', 'clube atletico mineiro': 'atletico mg',\n    'atletico goianiense': 'atletico go', 'atletico goianiense go': 'atletico go',\n    'atletico paranaense': 'atletico pr', 'atletico paranaense pr': 'atletico pr',\n    'athletico paranaense': 'atletico pr', 'athletico paranaense pr': 'atletico pr', 'athletico pr': 'atletico pr', 'athletico': 'atletico pr',\n    'sport recife': 'sport', 'sport club do recife': 'sport', 'sport recife pe': 'sport',\n    'ceara sporting club': 'ceara', 'ceara sc': 'ceara', 'clube do remo': 'remo',\n    'nautico capibaribe': 'nautico', 'nautico capibaribe pe': 'nautico',\n    'vasco da gama': 'vasco', 'vasco da gama rj': 'vasco', 'cs alagoano': 'csa', 'cs sergipe': 'sergipe',\n    'boavista sport club': 'boavista', 'boavista sport club rj': 'boavista', 'boavista sc saquarema': 'boavista',\n    'gremio rs': 'gremio', 'internacional rs': 'internacional',\n    'vitoria ec': 'vitoria ba', 'ec vitoria': 'vitoria ba', 'vitoria': 'vitoria ba', 'ec bahia': 'bahia',\n    'red bull bragantino': 'bragantino', 'rb bragantino': 'bragantino', 'red bull bragantino sp': 'bragantino',\n    'botafogo': 'botafogo rj', 'sport club corinthians paulista': 'corinthians', 'spfc': 'sao paulo',\n    'parana clube': 'parana', 'santa cruz fc': 'santa cruz', 'aa ponte preta': 'ponte preta',\n    'america fc natal': 'america rn', 'novorizontino': 'novorizontino', 'gremio novorizontino': 'novorizontino',\n    'athletic club': 'athletic mg', 'fortaleza ec': 'fortaleza', 'fortaleza fc': 'fortaleza',\n    'sao jose poa': 'sao jose rs', 'operario fc ms': 'operario ms', 'ad confianca': 'confianca',\n    'vila nova fc': 'vila nova', 'sampaio correa ma': 'sampaio correa',\n}\nBASES = {'palmeiras','flamengo','corinthians','santos','sao paulo','sport','bahia','ceara','fortaleza','cruzeiro','coritiba','parana','chapecoense','avai','figueirense','criciuma','goias','gremio','internacional','fluminense','guarani','portuguesa','juventude','caxias','nautico','remo','paysandu','sampaio correa','csa','crb','abc','vasco','vila nova','ponte preta','santa cruz','joinville','bragantino','america rn','confianca','operario ms'}\ndef key(t):\n    s = slug(t)\n    if s in ALIASES: return ALIASES[s]\n    toks = s.split()\n    if toks and toks[-1].upper() in UF:\n        base = ' '.join(toks[:-1])\n        if base in BASES: return base\n    return s\n\ndef load(path, hcol, acol, hg, ag, dcol, dparse, scol=None, tcol=None, tval=None, comp=None):\n    rows = []\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n            if tcol and row[tcol] != tval: continue\n            try:\n                hgi, agi = int(float(row[hg])), int(float(row[ag]))\n            except (ValueError, TypeError):\n                hgi = agi = None\n            d = dparse(row[dcol]) if row[dcol] else None\n            s = int(row[scol]) if scol and row[scol] not in ('','NA') else (int(d[:4]) if d else None)\n            if s is None: continue\n            rows.append((d, key(row[hcol]), key(row[acol]), hgi, agi, s, comp))\n    return rows\n\ndef iso(d): return d[:10]\ndef brd(d):\n    dd, mm, yy = d.split('/'); return f\"{yy}-{mm}-{dd}\"\n\nmatches = []\nmatches += load('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv','home_team','away_team','home_goal','away_goal','datetime',iso,scol='season',comp='Serie A')\nmatches += load('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv','home_team','away_team','home_goal','away_goal','datetime',iso,scol='season',comp='Copa do Brasil')\nmatches += load('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv','home_team','away_team','home_goal','away_goal','datetime',iso,scol='season',comp='Libertadores')\nmatches += load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv','home','away','home_goal','away_goal','date',iso,tcol='tournament',comp=None)  # per-tournament below\n\nwith open('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n        try:\n            hgi, agi = int(float(row['home_goal'])), int(float(row['away_goal']))\n        except (ValueError, TypeError):\n            hgi = agi = None\n        d = row['date'][:10]\n        matches.append((d, key(row['home']), key(row['away']), hgi, agi, int(d[:4]), row['tournament']))\n\nmatches += load('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv','Equipe_mandante','Equipe_visitante','Gols_mandante','Gols_visitante','Data',brd,scol='Ano',comp='Serie A')\nprint(\"total matches:\", len(matches))\n\n# biggest wins (scored, all comps)\nscored = [m for m in matches if m[3] is not None]\nbig = sorted(scored, key=lambda m: (-abs(m[3]-m[4]), -(m[3]+m[4])))[:8]\nfor b in big: print(\"BIG:\", b)\n\n# Fla-Flu h2h (all comps, dedup by season/home/away/score)\nseen = set(); h2h = []\nfor m in matches:\n    if {m[1],m[2]} == {'flamengo','fluminense'}:\n        k = (m[5], m[1], m[2], m[3], m[4], m[6])\n        if k in seen: continue\n        seen.add(k); h2h.append(m)\nfla = sum(1 for m in h2h if (m[1]=='flamengo' and m[3]>m[4]) or (m[2]=='flamengo' and m[4]>m[3]))\nflu = sum(1 for m in h2h if (m[1]=='fluminense' and m[3]>m[4]) or (m[2]=='fluminense' and m[4]>m[3]))\ndr = len(h2h) - fla - flu\nprint(f\"Fla-Flu: {len(h2h)} matches, Flamengo {fla}, Fluminense {flu}, draws {dr}\")\n\n# Corinthians home 2022 (Serie A from brfile only)\ncor = [m for m in matches if m[6]=='Serie A' and m[5]==2022 and m[1]=='corinthians' and m[3] is not None and m[0] and m[0]<'2023' and m[0]>='2022']\n# oops brfile rows only - need source tracking; skip precision, just count from brfile-style: use season col rounds... let me just count home wins for corinthians 2022 from brfile alone\nEOF","time":{"start":1788273988282,"end":1788273988285}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All Copa do Brasil big names use \"Name - UF\" format which suffix-strips correctly (e.g. \"Vasco da Gama - RJ\" → 'vasco da gama rj' → needs alias → 'vasco'). Libertadores Brazilian names are clean, plus bare 'Athletico' (aliased) and 'Botafogo' (bare → alias to 'botafogo rj').\n\nNow I have everything to build. Final architecture:\n\n**brazilian_soccer/normalize.py**\n- `BRAZILIAN_STATE_CODES`\n- `slug(name)` \n- `ALIASES` dict (slug → canonical key) — comprehensive table from analysis\n- `UNAMBIGUOUS_BASES` (BASES) set\n- `team_key(name)` \n- `parse_date(s)` → date | None (ISO, ISO+time, DD/MM/YYYY)\n- DERBY definitions (pairs of canonical keys + names)\n\n**brazilian_soccer/models.py**\n- `Match` dataclass: date, home, away, home_goals, away_goals, season, competition, stage, round, source, extras(dict)\n- `Player` dataclass: id, name, age, nationality, overall, potential, club, position, jersey, height, weight, foot, skills subset\n- `TeamRecord` dataclass: team, played, wins, draws, losses, gf, ga, points\n\n**brazilian_soccer/data.py**\n- `SourceSpec` constants for the 6 files\n- loaders per file → list[Match] / list[Player]\n- `Dataset` class: loads all, builds indexes:\n  - matches (list), deduped_matches (for display)\n  - by_team: dict[key → list[Match]]\n  - competitions: dict[name → dict[season → dict[source → count]]]\n  - canonical source resolution for league tables (`league_source(competition, season)`)\n  - players, players_by_club\n  - display names: most-common raw + curated overrides\n  - brazilian_clubs set (teams in domestic comps)\n- module-level `load_dataset(data_dir=...)` with `functools.lru_cache` for reuse\n\n**brazilian_soccer/query.py** — pure functions taking Dataset:\n- search_matches(...)\n- last_match_between(a, b)\n- head_to_head(a, b, competition, season)\n- team_stats(team, competition, season, venue)\n- best_records(competition, season, venue, min_matches, limit)\n- team_competitions(team)\n- search_players(...), top_players(...), players_by_club(...)\n- standings(competition, season), relegation_zone(...)\n- champion(competition, season)\n- bracket(competition, season)\n- competition_overview()\n- average_goals(competition, season, team)\n- biggest_wins(competition, season, team, limit)\n- derbies(season)\n- season_comparison(competition, a, b)\n- team_profile(team)\n\nEach returns plain data structures (dicts/lists) OR formatted strings? Better: query functions return STRUCTURED data; server.py formats into the nice text. Tests assert on structured data (BDD \"Then I should receive a list of matches / each match should have date, scores, and competition\"). \n\n**brazilian_soccer/server.py**\n- builds MCPServer, registers tools that call query functions and format text like the spec examples.\n\n**main.py** — entry point (stdio).\n\n**tests/** — conftest with `dataset` fixture (session-scoped), BDD GWT tests.\n\nAlso `requirements.txt` (mcp>=2), `pytest.ini`/pyproject minimal, README update.\n\nFormatting decisions for tools (mirror spec examples):\n- search_matches → list lines \"2023-09-03: Flamengo 2-1 Fluminense (Brasileirão Round 22)\" + total count + note. Head-to-head included when both team & opponent given.\n- team_stats → \"Corinthians home record (2022 Brasileirão):\" block.\n- standings → numbered table with pts, W/D/L, GF/GA, GD, champion marker, relegation zone marker.\n- players → numbered list like example.\n- etc.\n\nNow let me think about `team_stats` numbers example: \"Corinthians home record (2022): Matches 19, W11 D5 L3, GF28 GA15, win rate 57.9%\" — matches actual 2022 Corinthians home record? Whatever the data says.\n\nCompetition display names: \"Brasileirão\" vs \"Serie A\"? I'll use friendly names: \"Serie A\" → \"Brasileirão Série A\"? The examples say \"Brasileirão Round 22\". I'll name competitions:\n- \"Serie A\" (canonical), display \"Brasileirão Série A\"\n- \"Serie B\" → \"Brasileirão Série B\"\n- \"Serie C\" → \"Brasileirão Série C\"\n- \"Copa do Brasil\"\n- \"Libertadores\" → \"Copa Libertadores\"\nTool param `competition` accepts fuzzy: \"brasileirao\", \"serie a\", \"serie-a\", \"copa do brasil\", \"libertadores\", \"brazilian cup\", etc. — implement `resolve_competition(name)` with slug matching + keywords.\n\nTeam param: `resolve_team(name)` — team_key(name) exact → else prefix/substring search over known keys/display names → if multiple matches, return ambiguity error listing them (nice MCP behavior); if none, error. E.g. \"atletico\" → ambiguous (atletico mg, atletico pr, atletico go) → error listing. \n\nFor search_matches `team` + `opponent`: resolve both.\n\nDate params: accept \"YYYY-MM-DD\", \"DD/MM/YYYY\", \"YYYY\" (year). parse via parse_date; year → date range.\n\nStage param: \"final\", \"semifinal\", \"quarterfinal\", \"round of 16\", \"group stage\" — case-insensitive match against Match.stage; for Copa, stages computed at load (final/semifinal/quarterfinal/round of 16/round N via the ≤2/≤4/≤8/≤16 heuristic per season).\n\nAlright — Match.stage for Copa: compute per season: rounds sorted; last round r_max: matches_in_round ≤ 2 → \"final\"; r_max-1 ≤4 → \"semifinal\"; r_max-2 ≤8 → \"quarterfinal\"; r_max-3 ≤16 → \"round of 16\"; else \"round N\". But CAREFUL: 2021 (max r4=16 matches): r4 → not final (16 > 2); r3=32 → nothing; so stages = \"Round 4\"... good. And keep `round` field as the raw round number for display \"(Copa do Brasil Round 8)\".\n\nFor Brasileirão matches, stage=None, round=number → display \"Round 22\".\n\nDedup for display (search_matches): key = (competition, season, home, away, home_goals, away_goals) — hmm wait, one more edge: BRFB 2020 Serie A (partial) + brfile 2020 (full): BRFB-only matches (missing from brfile?) — 264 vs 380: BRFB has matches brfile lacks? If dates/scores match they dedup; BRFB-only ones would add as extra rows → a 2020 \"all matches\" search could show >380 with near-dupes. Acceptable: search listing shows sources; and I'll sort by date. Fine.\n\nWait, actually also — BRFB home/away might be FLIPPED vs brfile for the same match (venue recorded differently)? Score agreement 2573/2633 with my (home,away)-keyed match — keyed on (season, home, away) so agreement test already required same home team ✓. Good.\n\nFIFA player parsing details: ID, Name, Age, Nationality, Overall, Potential, Club, Position, Jersey Number, Preferred Foot, Height, Weight + skill ratings (Crossing, Finishing, Dribbling, ...). Some rows have empty Position ('' seen) → keep as \"\". Club empty → None (free agents). Age/Overall/Potential/Jersey → int where parseable. Height \"5'7\", Weight \"159lbs\" — keep raw strings. Skills → int where parseable, store in `skills: dict[str,int]`. Player.key for club: team_key(club).\n\nWait — one more check: FIFA 'Name' — \"L. Messi\". Search by name substring case-insensitive. \"Who is Gabriel Barbosa?\" → not found → friendly message. OK.\n\nplayers_by_club (Brazilian players at Brazilian clubs): group FIFA players by club_key where club_key ∈ brazilian_clubs; filter nationality=\"Brazil\"; output per club: count + avg overall. The example shows \"Flamengo: 8 players (avg rating 74)\" — in FIFA 19, Flamengo absent; real output will show Grêmio etc. — data-driven.\n\nHmm — actually WAIT. Let me double-check the FIFA dataset version — 18,207 players with L. Messi 31yo at Barcelona → FIFA 19. Brazilian clubs present: the 14 listed. 827 Brazilians. For \"top Brazilian players\": Neymar 92 ✓ matches spec example.\n\nbrazilian_clubs set: teams appearing in domestic competitions across match files = teams from Serie A/B/C, Copa do Brasil, novo, brfile. Libertadores-only teams (Boca etc.) excluded. But note: some Brazilian clubs appear ONLY in Libertadores data? E.g. \"Barueri\"? no. Libertadores-only Brazilians: \"Athletico\" ✓ appears in Serie A too. Fine.\n\nOne more subtlety — `TeamRecord` for standings of cups: skip. `standings` only for league comps (Serie A/B/C); for cups, return friendly error suggesting `champion`/`bracket`.\n\n`average_goals`: over scored matches; also home win rate / draw rate / away win rate (spec example shows \"Home win rate: 47.3%\").\n\n`biggest_wins`: rank by abs goal diff, then by total goals; show top N with margin.\n\n`season_comparison(competition, season_a, season_b)`: for each: matches, avg goals, home win %, champion, top scorer team, biggest win.\n\n`team_profile(team)`: display name, aliases (raw variants), competitions+seasons, overall W/D/L, GF/GA, best season finish?, plus players at club from FIFA (top 5 by overall). Cross-file ✓.\n\n`derbies(season=None)`: all matches between derby pairs (+ season filter), with derby names.\n\n`last_match_between(team_a, team_b)`: most recent by date (and within same date, latest source). Return match + note.\n\n`champion(competition, season)`:\n- League: standings[0] → champion + points + note \"calculated from N matches\".\n- Libertadores: stage==\"final\" matches → aggregate; winner or \"tied on aggregate, decided on penalties (not in dataset)\"; if no final in data → say so.\n- Copa do Brasil: stage==\"final\" (computed) → same aggregate logic.\n\n`bracket(competition, season)`: knockout rounds (stage in final/semifinal/quarterfinal/round of 16) grouped by stage, ties aggregated: for each pair, list agg score + winner. Order stages from early to late. For Copa early rounds (rounds 1-4 with many matches) — bracket should show ALL knockout rounds? Copa is entirely knockout: rounds 1..8. \"Show the 2018 Copa Libertadores bracket\" — Libertadores knockout: round of 16 → final. I'll implement bracket for any competition: group matches by stage (or round) and aggregate ties. For big rounds (Copa rounds 1-4, 32+ matches) it gets long — cap output and note. Actually let me define bracket = stages: final, semifinals, quarterfinals, round of 16 (i.e., \"late\" knockout). For Copa do Brasil those labels exist via my computed stages for the last 4 rounds only... hmm my heuristic labels only when counts ≤16; rounds 1-3 of modern Copa (40-80 teams) → \"Round 1/2/3\". So bracket for Copa shows: Round of 16? r5=16 matches → labeled \"round of 16\" ✓, r6 QF ✓, r7 SF ✓, r8 final ✓. So bracket = last 4 rounds for Copa — good summary. For Libertadores: round of 16 (8 ties), QF, SF, final ✓.\n\nTie aggregation: matches between same pair (any venue) in same stage+season → two legs; aggregate goals; winner = higher agg; tie → \"penalties (not in dataset)\". Single match → winner or draw note. Note: Copa 2020 final: Grêmio 0-1 Palmeiras + Palmeiras 2-0 Grêmio → agg 1-3 Palmeiras ✓.\n\nEdge: knockout ties where teams meet twice in same stage with SAME home team twice (rare) — aggregation by pair still works (sum goals per team across the 2 matches regardless of venue) ✓.\n\n`relegation`: standings includes bottom-4 marker for Serie A/B. Spec Q: \"Which teams were relegated in 2020?\" → standings output shows \"Relegation zone (bottom 4)\" or I add a `relegated(competition, season)` helper — I'll include it in standings text and also make champion tool mention relegated. Actually cleaner: standings text marks Z: prefix or annotation on bottom 4 (Serie A/B only: relegation = bottom 4).\n\nPerformance: all queries are in-memory scans over ≤24k matches — milliseconds. Load time ~1s. ✓ meets <2s/<5s.\n\nMCP server tests: \n- list_tools returns ≥15 tools\n- call_tool(\"search_matches\", {...}) returns text containing expected substrings\n- call_tool with bad team → is_error or friendly message (I'll return friendly text; MCP ToolError for unknown team might mark is_error — fine either way; test for graceful handling: assert it returns something containing \"not found\" or is_error True).\n\nError handling in tools: catch TeamNotFound/CompetitionNotFound/AmbiguousTeam exceptions → return friendly string (not raise) so the LLM client gets a helpful message. I'll define exceptions in query.py.\n\nNow — the tool arg schema: FastMCP/MCPServer generates schema from type hints + docstring. Params with defaults are optional. Use `int | None = None` etc. Season param: `int | None`. Dates: `str | None` (parse inside). \n\nStructured outputs: return `str` → text content. Keep `structured_output=False`? Default auto-detect from return annotation `-> str` gives unstructured text ✓ (with maybe structured wrapper {'result': ...} — the earlier probe returned structured_content={'result': 'sum=5'} alongside text. Fine.)\n\nBDD test structure — pytest classes:\n\n```python\nclass TestScenarioFindMatchesBetweenTwoTeams:\n    \"\"\"Feature: Match Queries\n\n    Scenario: Find matches between two teams\n        Given the match data is loaded\n        When I search for matches between \"Flamengo\" and \"Fluminense\"\n        Then I should receive a list of matches\n        And each match should have date, scores, and competition\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def test_given_loaded_match_data_when_searching_flamengo_vs_fluminense_then_matches_have_date_scores_competition(self, dataset):\n        # Given\n        assert dataset.total_matches > 0\n        # When\n        result = query.search_matches(dataset, team=\"Flamengo\", opponent=\"Fluminense\")\n        # Then\n        assert result[\"total\"] > 0\n        for m in result[\"matches\"]:\n            assert m[\"date\"] is not None\n            assert m[\"competition\"]\n            ...\n```\n\nGWT via comments/structure. I'll write comprehensive scenarios covering all 5 categories + normalization + server. Let me count scenarios to hit ≥20 sample questions — I'll include a `test_sample_questions.py` mapping 20+ spec questions to tool calls (the \"Data Coverage: At least 20 sample questions can be answered\" criterion!) — each test asserts a meaningful, data-verified answer. That directly satisfies the success criteria.\n\nLet me nail down expected values for tests (from data, verified above):\n- 2019 Serie A champion: Flamengo 90 pts (28W 6D 4L) ✓\n- 2020 relegated: Coritiba, Botafogo, Vasco, Goiás (bottom 4 by points: Botafogo 27, Coritiba 31, Goiás 37, Vasco 41) ✓\n- 2015 champion Corinthians 81 ✓ (both sources agree)\n- 2022 champion: Palmeiras (via BRFB 379 matches) ✓\n- 2021 champion: Atlético-MG 84 ✓\n- Libertadores 2019 final: Flamengo 2-1 River Plate (single leg) ✓\n- Libertadores 2018 final: River Plate agg 5-3 ✓\n- Copa do Brasil 2013 final: Flamengo agg 3-1 Atlético-PR ✓\n- Copa do Brasil 2020 final: Palmeiras agg 3-1 Grêmio ✓\n- Copa do Brasil 2015 final: agg 2-2 tie → penalties note ✓\n- Fla-Flu H2H: computed from data (count wins) — assert consistency: wins_a + wins_b + draws == total; and total > 20.\n- Biggest win: need actual data value — compute during test authoring? Better: assert structural properties (margin ≥ 5, sorted desc) + known example: \"Santos 8-0 Bolivar\"?? that was in the SPEC example (\"2012-05-27: Santos 8-0 Bolivar (Libertadores)\") — but our Libertadores data starts 2013! So that example isn't in our data. I'll compute the real biggest wins from data and spot-check one known: Palmeiras 6-0 something? I'll verify at test time by computing — tests will assert structural invariants + a couple of hardcoded facts I verify now-ish during test writing. Let me compute biggest wins quickly when writing tests — I'll run a probe before finalizing assertions.\n- Average goals Serie A ≈ 2.4-2.5 — assert 2.0 < avg < 3.0.\n- FIFA: Neymar Jr 92, top Brazilian; Grêmio has 20 players; Brazilian players at Brazilian clubs include Grêmio with 20 (all-Brazilian? no — Grêmio squad in FIFA 19 has some foreigners; count from data).\n- \"Players at Flamengo\" → 0 with friendly note (data honesty) — test asserts graceful \"no players found\" not crash.\n- Date range query: matches in May 2019.\n- \"What matches did Palmeiras play in 2023?\" → Serie A 2023 (BRFB) ~37 matches + Copa do Brasil 2023 ✓.\n- Team competitions for Palmeiras: Serie A, Copa do Brasil, Libertadores ✓.\n- Derbies 2023: includes Gre-nal? 2023 Serie A has Internacional & Grêmio ✓ → at least a few derby matches; check Choque-Rei etc.\n- last_match_between(\"Flamengo\",\"Corinthians\") → returns a match with date + score (latest in dataset: 2023 Serie A or Copa 2023).\n- Corinthians home record 2022: compute expected at authoring.\n\nAlright — also the `stage` heuristic needs matches counts per (season, round) computed at load — fine.\n\nOne more decision: dataset caching for tests + server. `load_dataset(path)` with lru_cache keyed by resolved path. Server startup: `create_server()` builds MCPServer and registers tools with closure over 