{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788274196716,"sessionID":"ses_fa29f8b64ffekf1eHikDs909KG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_ccc434ce999f4e3c9b9c23b6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-xcxq6pfm/retort-63e205aaecc3/brazilian_soccer/__init__.py","content":"\"\"\"Brazilian Soccer MCP server package.\n\nProvides a Model Context Protocol server exposing a query interface over\nBrazilian soccer datasets (matches, teams, players, competitions) loaded\nfrom the CSV files in ``data/kaggle``.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom brazilian_soccer.data import Dataset, load_dataset\n\n__all__ = [\"Dataset\", \"load_dataset\"]\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-xcxq6pfm/retort-63e205aaecc3/brazilian_soccer/__init__.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/__init__.py","time":{"start":1788274196708,"end":1788274196714}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All expected values confirmed:\n- Corinthians home 2022 (BRFB canonical): 19 matches, 12W 4D 3L, GF 24, GA 11, 63.2% win rate\n- Serie A avg goals ≈ 2.355, home win rate ≈ 48.7%\n\nNow I'll write the implementation. Files:\n\n1. `brazilian_soccer/__init__.py`\n2. `brazilian_soccer/normalize.py` — slug, ALIASES, BASES, team_key, parse_date, DERBIES\n3. `brazilian_soccer/models.py` — Match, Player, TeamRecord\n4. `brazilian_soccer/data.py` — loaders + Dataset + canonical source resolution + display names\n5. `brazilian_soccer/query.py` — query engine + exceptions\n6. `brazilian_soccer/server.py` — MCPServer + tools + formatters\n7. `main.py`\n8. `tests/conftest.py` + test files\n9. `requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml`\n10. README.md update\n\nLet me write normalize.py first. Design details:\n\n```python\ndef team_key(name): ...  # canonical key\ndef parse_date(value): ...  # -> date | None\ndef slug(name): ...\n```\n\nDerbies as list of (team_a, team_b, name). Team keys for derbies:\n- flamengo/fluminense \"Fla-Flu\"\n- flamengo/vasco \"Clássico dos Milhões\"\n- botafogo rj/fluminense \"Clássico Vovô\"\n- botafogo rj/flamengo \"Clássico da Rivalidade\"\n- botafogo rj/vasco \"Clássico dos Gigantes\"\n- gremio/internacional \"Gre-Nal\"\n- corinthians/sao paulo \"Clássico Majestoso\"\n- sao paulo/santos \"Choque-Rei\"\n- corinthians/palmeiras \"O Derby (Derby Paulista)\"\n- palmeiras/santos \"Clássico da Saudade\"\n- atletico mg/cruzeiro \"Clássico Mineiro\"\n- bahia/vitoria ba \"Ba-Vi\"\n- sport/nautico \"Clássico dos Clássicos\"\n- sport/santa cruz \"Clássico das Multidões\"\n- nautico/santa cruz \"Clássico dos Emoções\"\n- coritiba/atletico pr \"Atletiba\"\n- atletico pr/parana \"Paratiba\"\n- ceara/fortaleza \"Clássico-Rei\"\n- remo/paysandu \"Re-Pa\"\n- avai/figueirense \"Clássico de Florianópolis\"\n- goias/vila nova \"Clássico Goiano\"\n- cruzeiro/america mg \"Clássico das Emoções\"? — hmm, Cruzeiro×América-MG is \"Clássico das Emoções\"? No — that's Náutico×Santa Cruz. Cruzeiro x América is \"o Clássico de Mineirão\"? Not standard. Skip.\n\nCopa do Brasil stage heuristic (per season): rounds sorted desc by number; label r_max \"final\" if count ≤2; r_max-1 \"semifinal\" if count ≤4; r_max-2 \"quarterfinal\" if count ≤8; r_max-3 \"round of 16\" if count ≤16. Others: \"Round N\". Store stage for all Copa matches. Note: 2012 has only 6 rounds → r6=2 → final ✓, r5=4 → SF ✓, r4=8 → QF ✓, r3=16 → round of 16 ✓ (2012 r3 had 16 matches ✓).\n\nLibertadores: stage from file: \"group stage\", \"round of 16\", \"quarterfinals\", \"semifinals\", \"final\" — normalize display: \"Group stage\", \"Round of 16\", \"Quarterfinals\", \"Semifinals\", \"Final\". Keep raw for matching (case-insensitive).\n\nFor Serie A/B: stage=None, round=N → display \"(Round N)\".\nBRFB: no round/stage → display \"(stats incl. corners...)\" no — display just competition.\n\nMatch.display label helper in formatting.\n\nNow data.py — Dataset:\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass CompetitionInfo:\n    name: str\n    display: str\n    kind: 'league' | 'cup'\n    seasons: dict[int, dict[str, int]]  # season -> {source: match_count}\n```\n\nSources:\n- SOURCE_BRASILEIRAO = \"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\"\n- SOURCE_CUP = \"Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\"\n- SOURCE_LIBERTADORES = \"Libertadores_Matches.csv\"\n- SOURCE_BRFB = \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\"\n- SOURCE_NOVO = \"novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\"\n- SOURCE_FIFA = \"fifa_data.csv\"\n\nCOMPETITIONS registry:\n- \"Serie A\": league, sources: [Brasileirao (2012-2022), Novo (2003-2019), BRFB Serie A (2014-2023)]\n- \"Serie B\": league, [BRFB]\n- \"Serie C\": league, [BRFB]\n- \"Copa do Brasil\": cup, [Cup file, BRFB]\n- \"Libertadores\": cup, [Libertadores file]\n\nCompetition resolution (query side): accepts aliases: 'serie a', 'seriea', 'brasileirao', 'brasileirão série a', 'a series'... implement `resolve_competition(name)`: slug the input; check startswith/contains mapping:\n- contains 'libertadores' → Libertadores\n- contains 'copa do brasil' or equals 'brazilian cup' or ('copa' and 'brasil') → Copa do Brasil\n- contains 'serie b'/'série b'/'b' → hmm careful. Order: check 'serie c' first, then 'serie b', then 'serie a' or 'brasileir' → Serie A.\n- slug 'serie a' or 'brasileirao' or 'brasileirao serie a' etc.\n\nCanonical source selection `canonical_source(comp, season)`:\n```python\ndef canonical_source(comp, season):\n    candidates = [(source, matches) for source with matches in (comp, season)]\n    league: filter out polluted (any team count > 2*(n_teams-1))\n    pick max by (scored_matches, -priority_index)\n```\nNeed per-source scored counts + team counts. I'll compute in Dataset: `league_tables` cache: dict[(comp, season)] → (source_used, matches_used, table). Compute lazily + cache.\n\nTeam match count per source per season: count home+away per team.\n\nFor cups: canonical = priority source with most matches (Cup file first).\n\n`deduped_matches`: for display queries. Build once: sort matches by (source_priority), keep first per key (competition, season, home, away, home_goals, away_goals) — but only dedupe within same competition! Note competitions are canonical across sources (\"Serie A\" from 3 sources, \"Copa do Brasil\" from 2, \"Libertadores\" from 1). ✓.\n\nHmm — one catch: dedup with home_goals=None (unscored): key includes None — brfile 2022 NA rows vs BRFB scored rows for same fixture → different keys → both shown. E.g. \"Palmeiras 2022 matches\" — the NA brfile row (Palmeiras vs Atletico-GO NA-NA) AND BRFB's scored version both appear! Ugly. Better dedup: (competition, season, home, away) ONLY for LEAGUE matches (unique fixture in league), plus score-tiebreak for cups. League fixtures: home/away unique per season ✓. Cup: same pairing can meet twice with same home → include score+date? For cups I'll use (comp, season, stage_or_round, home, away) — two legs differ by round/stage ✓ (Copa rounds distinguish legs; Libertadores stages). If same stage+same home twice (weird) → add date. Let me use key = (comp, season, round_or_stage, home, away) for all: league round present in brfile/novo; BRFB has no round → key ('', home, away) — BRFB league rows would NOT dedupe against brfile rows (different round key)!! Damn.\n\nOK compromise: key = (comp, season, home, away, first_distinguisher) where distinguisher = round/stage if present else goals-signature... no wait. Let me think again:\n\nLeague: fixture uniquely (comp, season, home, away) — UNLESS playoffs (2003/2004 novo had playoffs? 552 matches, 24 teams, 46 games each = pure round robin ✓ no playoffs... but wait, 2003 was actually decided with playoffs IRL — but data shows 46 rounds round-robin, fine).\n- So league dedup key: (comp, season, home, away) ✓ — merges brfile+novo+BRFB perfectly; keeps NA-vs-scored as ONE row (priority source order decides which: brfile first → NA row kept, BRFB scored dropped — hmm! For 2022 that means showing NA score for a match BRFB has scored. Prefer scored rows! Sort candidates: scored first, then source priority. Then BRFB scored row wins over brfile NA row ✓, brfile scored wins over BRFB scored (priority) ✓.\n- 2003-2019: brfile scored wins over novo (same data anyway, 100% agreement) ✓.\n\nCup: two-legged ties = same (comp, season, home, away) can occur twice legitimately?? Copa: leg1 home A, leg2 home B → (home,away) differ ✓. BUT if both legs at same venue (e.g. pandemic single-venue or neutral finals): 2018 Copa final: Cruzeiro home leg1, Corinthians home leg2 ✓ differ. 2020: Grêmio leg1, Palmeiras leg2 ✓. Rare same-venue-twice: risk merging two distinct matches. Mitigate: cup dedup key = (comp, season, home, away, goals if not None else '') — matches with same score+venue merged only if truly identical (both NA? both same score — e.g. 2017 r7: Botafogo 0-0 Flamengo AND ... no). Let me use (comp, season, home, away, home_goals, away_goals) for cups — safe (identical scorelines at same venue in same season+comp are near-always the same match recorded twice across sources).\n\nSo: dedup key = league ? (comp, season, home, away) : (comp, season, home, away, hg, ag). Order candidates: (is_scored desc, source_priority asc). \n\nFor `matches_by_team` index used by search — build from deduped list ✓.\n\nStandings/team_stats: canonical single source per (comp, season) — never mixes → no double count ✓.\n\nlast_match_between / head_to_head: use deduped (multi-source, full coverage) ✓ — H2H across all comps is a display/record query, deduped view right. Fla-Flu test: 46 matches (computed above with similar dedup) ✓.\n\naverage_goals / biggest_wins: canonical per season when (comp, season) specified; when comp specified but season=None across seasons — mixing sources would double count! E.g. \"average goals in Brasileirão\" (no season): brfile 2012-2022 + novo 2003-2019 + BRFB 2014-2023 → triple count. Solution: compute per (comp, season) canonical, then aggregate the per-season numbers ✓. Same for biggest_wins (pool canonical matches across seasons). team_stats (no season): aggregate per-season canonical across seasons ✓.\n\nSo the core primitive: `canonical_matches(competition=None, season=None)` → for each (comp, season) present: canonical source's scored(+unscored?) matches; concat. If season given but comp None: all comps that season. If both None: all. This is THE query basis for stats. Unsored: include in listing queries, exclude from stats (functions filter on goals not None).\n\nLeague table: from canonical_matches(comp, season) scored → points table.\n\nCup champion/bracket: from canonical cup matches by stage.\n\nBrazilian clubs set: teams appearing in comps other than Libertadores (i.e., domestic comps: Serie A/B/C, Copa do Brasil — from any source) ✓.\n\nDisplay names: build from all raw names in match files + FIFA clubs: per key, Counter raw → pick best: prefer curated DISPLAY_OVERRIDES; else the most common; tie → with accents → shorter. Curated overrides for major clubs (~45).\n\nPlayer club key: team_key(club) — for FIFA \"Santos Laguna\" → 'santos laguna' (not Brazilian ✓ not in domestic set ✓).\n\nFIFA positions: group mapping for \"forwards\" queries? \"Show me all forwards from São Paulo FC\" — position param: exact match (ST, CF, LW, RW...) or group ('forward' → ST/CF/LW/RW/LS/RS/LF/RF; 'midfielder' → CM/CDM/CAM/LM/RM/...; 'defender' → CB/LB/RB/...; 'goalkeeper' → GK). I'll add `resolve_position` supporting groups. São Paulo FC isn't in FIFA data (graceful empty) — test with Santos instead: \"forwards from Santos\" ✓.\n\nOK — writing code now. One more thing: `parse_date` for season strings in tools: if user passes season=2023 → filter season field. from/to dates → parse_date (also accept bare year \"2023\" → 2023-01-01..2023-12-31? The season param covers years; keep dates strict: ISO or DD/MM/YYYY).\n\nLet me write the files. I'll be careful about: no comments per system prompt (docstrings OK — they're needed for MCP tool descriptions and are documentation, not comments).\n\nActually — re-reading the system prompt: \"IMPORTANT: DO NOT ADD ***ANY*** COMMENTS unless asked\". Docstrings for public functions = documentation. MCP tools REQUIRE descriptions. I'll use docstrings, no inline # comments.\n\nmodels.py:\n\n```python\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom datetime import date\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Match:\n    date: date | None\n    home: str\n    away: str\n    home_goals: int | None\n    away_goals: int | None\n    season: int | None\n    competition: str\n    source: str\n    stage: str | None = None\n    round: str | None = None\n    extras: dict = field(default_factory=dict, compare=False)\n\n    @property\n    def is_scored(self): ...\n    def involving(self, team): ...\n    def result_for(self, team): 'W' | 'L' | 'D' | None\n```\n\nPlayer:\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Player:\n    id, name, age, nationality, overall, potential, club, position, jersey, height, weight, foot, skills: dict\n```\n\nTeamRecord:\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass TeamRecord:\n    team, played, wins, draws, losses, goals_for, goals_against\n    points, goal_diff, win_rate properties\n```\n\nTable entry for standings: rank, record, marks (champion/relegation).\n\nNow data.py. The Dataset:\n\n```python\nclass Dataset:\n    def __init__(self, data_dir):\n        self.data_dir = Path(data_dir)\n        self.matches: list[Match] = []\n        self.players: list[Player] = []\n        self.display_names: dict[str, str] = {}\n        self._by_team: dict[str, list[Match]] = defaultdict(list)\n        self._by_club: dict[str, list[Player]] = defaultdict(list)\n        self.brazilian_clubs: set[str] = set()\n        self._deduped: list[Match] | None\n        self._canonical_cache: dict[tuple, list[Match]]\n        self._table_cache: dict[tuple, Table]\n        self._load_all()\n```\n\nLoaders:\n\n```python\ndef _load_brasileirao(self): ...  # season col, round col, states present but unused\ndef _load_copa_do_brasil(self): ...  # stage heuristic\ndef _load_libertadores(self): ...\ndef _load_br_football(self): ...  # tournament → comp; extras\ndef _load_novo(self): ...  # DD/MM/YYYY; Arena extra\ndef _load_fifa(self): ...\n```\n\nCompetition constants module-level in data.py:\n```python\nSERIE_A = \"Serie A\"; SERIE_B = \"Serie B\"; SERIE_C = \"Serie C\"\nCOPA_DO_BRASIL = \"Copa do Brasil\"; LIBERTADORES = \"Libertadores\"\nCOMPETITION_DISPLAY = {SERIE_A: \"Brasileirão Série A\", ...}\nCOMPETITION_KIND = {...: \"league\"/\"cup\"}\nSOURCE_PRIORITY = {brfile: 0, novo: 1, cup: 0, libertadores: 0, brfb: 2}\n```\n\nWait — source priority per competition. Global order fine: Brasileirao_Matches(0), Brazilian_Cup(0), Libertadores(0), novo(1), BRFB(2).\n\ncanonical_source(comp, season):\n```python\nseason_sources = [m for m in matches if m.competition == comp and m.season == season]\ngroup by source → count scored, teams count\nif league: exclude polluted sources (max team count > 2*(len(teams)-1)); if all polluted → pick least polluted (min overflow ratio) with caveat\npick max scored; tie → priority\n```\n\nWait, \"if all polluted\": e.g. Serie B 2021 (only BRFB, polluted) → use it + mark caveat. Compute overflow = max_team_count / cap.\n\nTable computation:\n```python\ndef league_table(comp, season) -> Table:\n    matches = canonical_matches(comp, season) scored\n    records per team; rank by (points, gd, gf, name)\n```\nRelegation zone = bottom 4 (Serie A/B).\n\nCup final detection:\n```python\ndef cup_finals(comp, season): matches with stage == 'final' (Copa computed, Libertadores file) \n```\n\nChampion:\n- league: table[0]\n- cup: aggregate finals; winner if agg differs else None (penalties note)\n\nBracket: group canonical cup matches by stage order ['round of 16','quarterfinals','semifinals','final'] + Copa 'Round N' stages? For Copa I set stage for last-4 rounds only; bracket shows stages present in that order; for stages named like 'round of 16'/'quarterfinals'/'semifinals'/'final'. Plus for Copa without those (2021) → show last available rounds as \"Round N\" listing ties. Implementation: collect knockout matches = stage in the 4 labels; if none → fallback: last 2 rounds by round number, group ties. Keep simpler: bracket lists all stages that are in KNOCKOUT_STAGES order present; if empty → message \"no knockout-stage matches in dataset for that season\" + suggest search_matches. Hmm — but Copa 2012 rounds 4,5,6 = QF/SF/Final ✓ labeled. 2021: no labels → message. Good enough + honest.\n\nTie aggregation for bracket:\n```python\ndef _aggregate_ties(matches):  # same season+stage, pair {a,b}\n    per pair: list legs; agg goals per team; winner or None\n```\n\nQueries in query.py — signatures (all take dataset first):\n\n```python\ndef search_matches(ds, *, team=None, opponent=None, competition=None, season=None,\n                   from_date=None, to_date=None, stage=None, team_side=\"any\", limit=20) -> dict\ndef last_match_between(ds, team_a, team_b) -> dict | None\ndef head_to_head(ds, team_a, team_b, *, competition=None, season=None, limit=10) -> dict\ndef team_stats(ds, team, *, competition=None, season=None, venue=\"all\") -> dict\ndef best_records(ds, *, competition=None, season=None, venue=\"all\", min_matches=10, limit=5) -> dict\ndef team_competitions(ds, team) -> dict\ndef team_profile(ds, team, limit_players=5) -> dict\ndef search_players(ds, *, name=None, club=None, nationality=None, position=None,\n                   min_overall=None, max_overall=None, limit=20) -> dict\ndef top_players(ds, *, club=None, nationality=None, position=None, limit=10) -> dict\ndef players_by_club(ds, *, nationality=None, only_brazilian_clubs=True, limit=15) -> dict\ndef standings(ds, competition=SERIE_A, season=None) -> dict\ndef champion(ds, competition, season) -> dict\ndef bracket(ds, competition, season) -> dict\ndef competition_overview(ds) -> dict\ndef average_goals(ds, *, competition=None, season=None, team=None) -> dict\ndef biggest_wins(ds, *, competition=None, season=None, team=None, limit=5) -> dict\ndef derbies(ds, *, season=None, team=None, limit=30) -> dict\ndef season_comparison(ds, competition, season_a, season_b) -> dict\n```\n\nReturn dicts with plain values; server.py formats. Exceptions: `TeamNotFoundError`, `AmbiguousTeamError`, `CompetitionNotFoundError`, `InvalidParameterError` (all subclass `QueryError`).\n\nresolve_team(ds, name):\n```python\nk = team_key(name)\nif k in ds.known_teams: return k\nmatches = [t for t in known if name-slug in t or t in name-slug or display contains name]\nif len == 1 → it; if >1 → AmbiguousTeamError(list); else TeamNotFoundError\n```\nknown_teams = keys with ≥1 match (by_team keys) — plus for player queries, club keys from FIFA not in match data (e.g. FIFA-only clubs like \"River Plate\"? no — River is in Libertadores ✓; e.g. \"Paraná\" ✓ in match data; \"Vitória\" ✓). Player club resolution uses same resolve over club keys ∪ team keys.\n\nresolve_competition(name): as designed.\n\nNow — server.py tool surface (17 tools):\n1. search_matches\n2. last_match_between\n3. head_to_head\n4. team_stats\n5. best_records\n6. team_competitions\n7. team_profile\n8. search_players\n9. top_players\n10. players_by_club\n11. standings\n12. champion\n13. bracket\n14. competition_overview\n15. average_goals\n16. biggest_wins\n17. derbies\n18. season_comparison\n\nEach wraps query fn in try/except QueryError → friendly text.\n\nFormatters produce the spec-style outputs.\n\nmain.py:\n```python\nfrom brazilian_soccer.server import create_server\ndef main():\n    create_server().run()\nif __name__ == \"__main__\": main()\n```\n\nDataset load path: default `data/kaggle` relative to repo root — compute from `Path(__file__).parent.parent / \"data\" / \"kaggle\"`, overridable via env `BRAZILIAN_SOCCER_DATA_DIR`.\n\nTests — conftest:\n```python\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef dataset():\n    return load_dataset()\n```\n\nTest fil