@@\n \n def _load_libertadores(self, raw_name_counts: Counter) -> None:\n     path = self.data_dir / SOURCE_LIBERTADORES\n     for row in _csv_rows(path):\n+        season = _to_int(row.get(\"season\"))\n+        if season is None:\n+            continue\n         home_raw = row[\"home_team\"]\n         away_raw = row[\"away_team\"]\n         raw_name_counts[home_raw] += 1\n         raw_name_counts[away_raw] += 1\n@@ -219,9 +222,9 @@\n             home=team_key(home_raw),\n             away=team_key(away_raw),\n             home_goals=_to_int(row.get(\"home_goal\")),\n             away_goals=_to_int(row.get(\"away_goal\")),\n-            season=_to_int(row.get(\"season\")),\n+            season=season,\n             competition=LIBERTADORES,\n             source=SOURCE_LIBERTADORES,\n             stage=(row.get(\"stage\") or \"\").strip().lower() or None,\n         ))\n","additions":4,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/data.py","time":{"start":1788274415236,"end":1788274415238}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Excellent! The data layer works:\n- 23,954 matches loaded, 17,259 deduplicated, 18,207 players\n- 2019 Serie A: Flamengo 90 pts ✓ (matches reality)\n- 2022: Palmeiras 81 from BRFB ✓\n- 2023: Grêmio 68 (best available data, honest)\n- Source selection works: 2021 → brfile (not polluted BRFB) ✓, 2023 → BRFB ✓, 2005 → novo ✓, 2022 → BRFB (more scored matches) ✓\n- Display names all good\n\nDedup: 17,259 from 23,954 — cross-source league dupes collapsed correctly (11×380 brfile/novo overlap + BRFB overlap etc.).\n\nWait, let me sanity-check dedup count: \n- Serie A: brfile 4180 + novo 6886 + BRFB Serie A 3689 = 14,755. Deduped Serie A should be: 2003-2011 novo only (9 seasons: 552+552+462+380×6 = 3556), 2012-2022 union (11×380 = 4180), 2023 BRFB (377) = 8,113.\n- Copa do Brasil: Cup file 1337 + BRFB Copa 1123 = 2460 → dedup by (season,home,away,score): overlap 2014-2021... say ~1800.\n- Libertadores: 1255.\n- Serie B: 3677, Serie C: 1807.\nTotal ≈ 8113 + 1800 + 1255 + 3677 + 1807 ≈ 16,652. Got 17,259 — close enough (my estimates rough). ✓ plausible.\n\n2019 bottom 4: Cruzeiro, Chapecoense, CSA, Avaí ✓ — actual 2019 relegated: Cruzeiro, Chapecoense, CSA, Avaí ✓✓ \n\nNow write query.py with all the query functions. Also fix: `canonical_source` caching bug — I use `self._source_cache[cache_key + (\"polluted\",)]` — that's a 3-tuple key vs 2-tuple keys — works since dict keys heterogeneous. Fine but slightly ugly; acceptable.\n\nOne issue in `canonical_matches`: when competition=None and season=None, it iterates competitions × seasons — pairs that don't exist produce empty selections — fine (canonical_source returns None → skip).\n\nBUT — canonical_source(comp, None-season)? No, seasons Counter keys are actual seasons present. OK.\n\nEdge: `seasons` Counter includes None season? Matches all have season != None (loaders skip or derive from date... wait BRFB season = match_date.year — always present; Libertadores NA-season row: season=None → still added to matches with season None! Let me check: Libertadores loader doesn't skip NA season rows — season=_to_int('NA')=None, goals NA→None. The match is included with season=None, date=parse_date('NA')=None. In canonical_source/league_table it's filtered by season match so never double counted. In dedup: key (comp, None, home, away, None, None) — kept. Harmless — actually wait: 'Flamengo vs Athletico NA final' — a phantom row. It would show in searches as an undated, unscored \"final\" match. Should I drop rows with no date AND no season AND no score? The row is junk (\"NA,NA,Flamengo,-,-,Athletico,final\"). Let me skip Libertadores rows where season is None entirely. Also the 2016 Chapecoense NA row: has date+season, no score — keep (real fixture). I'll add a skip in the Libertadores loader for season None. Also what about rows with date None but season present? e.g. any? Copa rows all have datetime. Fine.\n\nLet me patch that, then write query.py.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d76167f001lmSrKtvhu2mbjv","sessionID":"ses_fa29f8b64ffekf1eHikDs909KG","messageID":"msg_05d75bab7001nTgWC1nF6rpK7Q"}}
