arterfinal\": \"quarterfinal\",\n+    \"quarterfinals\": \"quarterfinal\",\n+    \"semifinal\": \"semifinal\",\n+    \"semifinals\": \"semifinal\",\n+    \"final\": \"final\",\n+    \"finals\": \"final\",\n+}\n+\n SKILL_COLUMNS = (\n     \"Crossing\", \"Finishing\", \"HeadingAccuracy\", \"ShortPassing\", \"Volleys\",\n     \"Dribbling\", \"Curve\", \"FKAccuracy\", \"LongPassing\", \"BallControl\",\n     \"Acceleration\", \"SprintSpeed\", \"Agility\", \"Reactions\", \"Balance\",\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-xcxq6pfm/retort-63e205aaecc3/brazilian_soccer/data.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-xcxq6pfm/retort-63e205aaecc3/brazilian_soccer/data.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-xcxq6pfm/retort-63e205aaecc3/brazilian_soccer/data.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-xcxq6pfm/retort-63e205aaecc3/brazilian_soccer/data.py\n@@ -69,8 +69,21 @@\n     \"semifinal\": \"Semifinals\",\n     \"final\": \"Final\",\n }\n \n+STAGE_ALIASES = {\n+    \"group stage\": \"group stage\",\n+    \"groups\": \"group stage\",\n+    \"round of 16\": \"round of 16\",\n+    \"last 16\": \"round of 16\",\n+    \"quarterfinal\": \"quarterfinal\",\n+    \"quarterfinals\": \"quarterfinal\",\n+    \"semifinal\": \"semifinal\",\n+    \"semifinals\": \"semifinal\",\n+    \"final\": \"final\",\n+    \"finals\": \"final\",\n+}\n+\n SKILL_COLUMNS = (\n     \"Crossing\", \"Finishing\", \"HeadingAccuracy\", \"ShortPassing\", \"Volleys\",\n     \"Dribbling\", \"Curve\", \"FKAccuracy\", \"LongPassing\", \"BallControl\",\n     \"Acceleration\", \"SprintSpeed\", \"Agility\", \"Reactions\", \"Balance\",\n","additions":13,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/data.py","time":{"start":1788274628430,"end":1788274628433}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Almost everything works. Issues found:\n\n1. **\"copa 2020: Palmeiras 0 - 3\"** — the goals_a/goals_b display is confusing: team_a = \"Grêmio\" (alphabetical: grêmio < palmeiras), so goals_a=0 (Grêmio), goals_b=3 (Palmeiras), champion Palmeiras ✓ correct but the print was misleading. Fine — server formatting will make it clear.\n\n2. **\"avg goals serie A: 8402 2.57 49.7\"** — 8402 matches?! That's summing canonical across (comp, season) — wait, canonical per season should give ~380 per season: 2003-2019 novo (17 seasons, but 2012-2019 brfile wins... wait no — canonical_source picks MOST SCORED: brfile 2012-2022 (380 each) vs novo 2012-2019 (380 each) — tie → priority → brfile. So Serie A canonical: 2003-2011 novo (9 seasons), 2012-2022 brfile (11), 2023 BRFB (1) = 21 seasons × ~380 = 7980 + extras. Hmm 8402. Let me compute: novo 2003: 552, 2004: 552, 2005: 462, 2006-2011: 380×6=2280 → 3846. brfile 2012-2022: 4180 (380×11). BRFB 2023: 377. Total = 3846+4180+377 = 8403 ≈ 8402 (one Libertadores NA row removed earlier doesn't affect). ✓ CORRECT! avg 2.57 goals, 49.7% home wins across 2003-2023 ✓ plausible.\n\nWait, but earlier I computed avg 2.355 for brfile-only (2012-2022). Now 2.57 for all seasons — the 2003-2011 era had more goals (2.6-2.7/game in early 2000s). Plausible ✓.\n\n3. **Grêmio top players**: \"Josué Chiamulera 83 LCB\" — these are real FIFA 19 Grêmio players? FIFA 19 Grêmio... Everton Cebolinha (82?), Luan (84?), Geromel (84)... Hmm — \"Josué Chiamulera\"?? That doesn't sound right. Wait — FIFA 19 Grêmio squad: the Brazilian clubs in FIFA 19 used GENERIC player names (fake names due to licensing!). Yes — FIFA 19's Brazilian clubs had fictional player names. So Neymar Jr (real, at PSG) is real, but Brazilian club squads use fake names. That's a data reality — fine for demo.\n\n4. **\"lib 2013: None | aggregate tied\"** ✓ honest.\n\n5. **bracket 2018 Libertadores round of 16**: 'Colo-Colo vs Corinthians 2-2 → winner None' — actual: Corinthians won on penalties ✓ honest reporting. Also \"Cruzeiro 2-1 Flamengo\" — actual 2018 R16: Cruzeiro beat Flamengo ✓. But WAIT — where are the quarterfinals?? 2018 bracket shows only \"round of 16\" and \"final\"! QF and SF missing! Let me check — Libertadores stage values: 'quarterfinals', 'semifinals' — KNOCKOUT_STAGES = (\"round of 16\", \"quarterfinal\", \"semifinal\", \"final\") — but the FILE uses \"quarterfinals\"/\"semifinals\" (plural!). My stage matching `m.stage in KNOCKOUT_STAGES` fails for plural forms! Need to normalize stage labels: map \"quarterfinals\"→\"quarterfinal\", \"semifinals\"→\"semifinal\" at load time. Let me fix in the Libertadores loader: stage = label.strip().lower().rstrip? No — map via dict: {\"quarterfinals\": \"quarterfinal\", \"semifinals\": \"semifinal\"}. Or simpler: strip trailing 's' from quarterfinal/semifinal? Cleanest: a small mapping.\n\n6. **copa finals search**: stage=\"final\" for Copa works ✓ (18 finals: 2 per season 2012-2020... 9 seasons × 2 = 18 ✓).\n\n7. **\"best away 2023\"**: Flamengo 47.4% ✓ plausible.\n\n8. **\"derbies 2023: 29\"** ✓.\n\n9. **team_competitions Palmeiras**: Série A 752 matches 2004-2023... wait Palmeiras was in Série B in 2013! But this only counts matches where Palmeiras appears — Série A 2004-2012 + 2014-2023 (no 2013 ✓ since they were in Serie B that year and BRFB Serie B 2013? BRFB starts 2014. So 2013 missing entirely — honest data). ✓\n\n10. **overview**: Copa do Brasil 1930 matches (dedup of 1337+1123 with overlap). Hmm — 1930. And \"Libertadores 1252\" (1255-1 NA row-2? Earlier file had 1256 lines = 1255 matches, minus 1 NA = 1254... shows 1252. Hmm — 2 lost? Let me think: Libertadores loader skips season None (1 row). 1255-1 = 1254. But dedup: cup dedup key = (comp, season, home, away, hg, ag) — two identical scorelines same venue same season merge! E.g. group stage: Flamengo hosts Peñarol twice in same season group? No... group stage has each pairing once per venue. But knockout two legs: leg 1 home A, leg 2 home B — different keys. Hmm, but identical (home, away, score) twice in same season+stage CAN happen in group stage? No — each pairing plays twice, one at each venue. Same venue twice = only if... let me not worry — 2 matches merged means there were 2 pairs of identical rows. Actually wait — could be genuinely duplicated rows in the file (same match recorded twice). That's what dedup is for. ✓ fine.\n\nHmm, actually let me double check one thing — the earlier probe with same dedup on Libertadores: I didn't. Whatever — 1252 vs 1254: 2 rows were exact duplicates in the source file. Acceptable.\n\n11. **avg goals \"all competitions\"** — works.\n\nLet me fix the Libertadores stage pluralization issue now. In `_load_libertadores`: stage = (row.get(\"stage\") or \"\").strip().lower() → then map:\n```python\n_LIBERTADORES_STAGE_MAP = {\n    \"group stage\": \"group stage\",\n    \"round of 16\": \"round of 16\",\n    \"quarterfinals\": \"quarterfinal\",\n    \"semifinals\": \"semifinal\",\n    \"final\": \"final\",\n}\n```\nActually generic: if stage endswith('s') and stage[:-1] in {'quarterfinal','semifinal'} → strip. I'll use a map for clarity.\n\nAlso — the same plural issue affects search_matches stage matching: Copa stages are singular already; Libertadores now singular ✓. And `wanted` map in search_matches handles \"quarterfinals\" input → \"quarterfinal\" ✓ and \"finals\" → \"final\" ✓.\n\nFix now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d79573e001bYdSXJuI8AlsOP","sessionID":"ses_fa29f8b64ffekf1eHikDs909KG","messageID":"msg_05d78d1a7001f5DQ5c4KUzeHfx"}}
