{"type":"text","timestamp":1788275124707,"sessionID":"ses_fa29f8b64ffekf1eHikDs909KG","part":{"id":"prt_05d80d0590014gethAKWjj6KAQ","messageID":"msg_05d80b8eb001UM2DFyBOPkip1Y","sessionID":"ses_fa29f8b64ffekf1eHikDs909KG","type":"text","text":"Done. **151 tests pass in 1.86s**, and the server was verified end-to-end with a real MCP stdio client handshake.\n\n## What was built\n\n**MCP server** (`mcp` v2 SDK, 18 tools) covering all five capability categories from TASK.md:\n\n| Category | Tools |\n|---|---|\n| Match | `search_matches` (team/opponent/competition/season/date-range/stage/home-away), `last_match_between`, `derbies` (21 named rivalries) |\n| Team | `team_stats`, `best_records`, `team_competitions`, `team_profile` (cross-file: match record + FIFA squad) |\n| Player | `search_players`, `top_players`, `players_by_club` (position groups, nationality, rating bounds) |\n| Competition | `standings` (points table + relegation zone), `champion`, `bracket` (aggregated knockout ties), `competition_overview` |\n| Statistics | `average_goals`, `biggest_wins`, `head_to_head`, `season_comparison` |\n\n**Key engineering decisions** (documented in README):\n- Three files overlap on Série A (2012-2022 / 2003-2019 / 2014-2023), so listings dedupe cross-source fixtures while standings use one **canonical source per season** — with a round-robin sanity check that rejects COVID-era \"2021\" data polluted by delayed 2020 matches\n- Team normalization handles `Palmeiras-SP` / `Palmeiras` / `Atlético Mineiro` / `Sport Club do Recife` variants while keeping `Atlético-MG/-PR/-GO` and `Botafogo-RJ/-SP/-PB` distinct; ambiguous names return candidate lists\n- Copa do Brasil finals detected structurally per season (format changed over years); two-legged finals aggregated, ties honestly reported as \"penalties, not in dataset\"\n- Verified against reality where the data allows: 2019 champion Flamengo 90pts, 2020 relegated Coritiba/Botafogo/Vasco/Goiás, 2019 Libertadores bracket fully correct\n\n**Tests**: BDD GWT-structured pytest (Gherkin docstrings per the spec's testing approach) — `tests/test_match_queries.py`, `test_team_queries.py`, `test_player_queries.py`, `test_competition_queries.py`, `test_statistics_queries.py`, `test_data_quality.py`, `test_mcp_server.py`, plus 28 end-to-end sample questions (spec requires ≥20), including the <2s/<5s performance budget.","time":{"start":1788275118169,"end":1788275124705}}}
